<p>Eight bodies were recovered along the central and eastern Mediterranean routes in Libya and Greece, underscoring the dangers of irregular sea crossings. A police officer quoted by Reuters said migrants’ bodies washed ashore east of Tripoli. In a separate incident off Greece, Al Jazeera reported three deaths as crossings continued.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Who was among the dead in Libya: The police officer said the bodies found in Libya included two women.</li><li>Where in Libya: The bodies were reported to have washed up in Qasr al-Akhyar, a coastal town east of Tripoli.</li><li>When it happened: The report was dated Feb 21, and the police officer spoke to Reuters on Saturday.</li><li>Libya count: The police officer said at least five migrants’ bodies were recovered in Libya.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Local residents in Libya: Residents said they saw a child’s body swept back out to sea by strong waves, prompting a coast guard search. (<a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/5-bodies-migrants-washed-ashore-east-libyas-capital-tripoli-police-officer-says-2026-02-21/'>Reuters</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera reporting: Al Jazeera said three people died in a separate incident off Greece as Mediterranean crossings continued. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/22/eight-bodies-found-in-libya-and-greece-as-mediterranean-crossings-continue'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/22/eight-bodies-found-in-libya-and-greece-as-mediterranean-crossings-continue'>Eight bodies recovered in Libya, Greece as Mediterranean death toll rises</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/5-bodies-of-migrants-washed-ashore-in-east-of-libyas-capital-tripoli-police-officer-says'>5 bodies of migrants washed ashore in east of Libya&#x27;s capital Tripoli, police officer says</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/5-bodies-migrants-washed-ashore-east-libyas-capital-tripoli-police-officer-says-2026-02-21/'>At least five bodies of refugees wash ashore near Tripoli, Libya. Residents also observe a child&#x27;s body carried back to sea by strong waves, prompting a coast guard search operation.</a> - reuters.com</li></ul>